@@@ note
Inline markup is re-serialised with its delimiters glued to its content. A link's '](url)'
tail is unbreakable, so the 30-column case overshoots rather than splitting the URL.

@@@ input
This is a paragraph with **bold**, *italic*, ~~struck~~ and a [link](https://example.com "Example") in it, long enough to wrap.

@@@ wrap 80
This is a paragraph with **bold**, *italic*, ~~struck~~ and a
[link](https://example.com "Example") in it, long enough to wrap.

@@@ wrap 30
This is a paragraph with
**bold**, *italic*, ~~struck~~
and a
[link](https://example.com "Example")
in it, long enough to wrap.

@@@ unwrap
This is a paragraph with **bold**, *italic*, ~~struck~~ and a [link](https://example.com "Example") in it, long enough to wrap.
